    "rationale": "The exhaustive optimizer-free V13 audit completed all 12368 start phases and reduced required-safety failures from the V12 count of 3440 to 2779 by seating declared sole contacts at zero clearance, but it retained 2372 hard impacts. Phase-to-artifact analysis found that the remaining impact probability rises sharply with the complete sole-normal tilt; the sagittal heel-to-forefoot closure is already effective while the lateral component remains dominant. A root-tilt prototype is rejected because changing support sides creates eight-to-twenty-five-degree target jumps, and an unconstrained five-joint per-frame projection is rejected because it changes most leg channels and exceeds the frozen acceleration admission bound. This identity preserves every V13 source, split, crop, BodySchema, USD, PD, contact, safety, terminal, velocity, joint-bound and ground-seating value. It adds an all-frame bilateral lateral-sole projection in the yaw-aligned root frame, using only hip roll and ankle roll under their existing bounds. Projecting both feet removes support-switch discontinuity; a ten-to-one inverse weight favors hip correction over the dynamically sensitive ankle channel, four bounded finite-difference iterations close the residual, and four symmetric delta-smoothing passes retain temporal continuity. The five-degree positive hip-roll floor continues to prevent adduction and thigh collision, and the plus-or-minus-five-degree ankle-roll range continues to retain the required fifteen-degree hard-ROM reserve. This is data-only remediation: optimizer execution remains forbidden until fresh deterministic import, native pose, formal visual and exhaustive zero-safety dynamic evidence all pass. The first complete V14 build locally validated all twenty-seven clips but observed only three bilateral contact cycles in the validation SlowWalk crop, so coverage remained failed. A bounded same-source crop check found that extending only cmu91-walk-slow-validation from source frame 1500 to 1650 yields exactly four bilateral cycles while retaining every local safety and trajectory bound: maximum protected acceleration is 15231600 microradians per second squared and maximum support-sole planar speed is 988647 micrometres per second. This V15 identity records that minimal extension within the same immutable 91/91_10 source and validation split group; all other inputs, algorithms, bounds and authorization remain unchanged."
